    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0402" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.512/73</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1263</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-11-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of the Legation’s despatch
                    No. 1215 of September 29 last on the subject of the so-called 99 Mercantile Tax
                    levied in Kiangsi Province, I have the honor to enclose herewith a further
                    despatch from the Consulate General at Hankow (No. 340) <pb facs="0403" n="237"
                        xml:id="pg237"/> under date of the 3d instant, reporting that the Kiukiang
                    branch of the Standard Oil Company has taken steps in pursuance of the
                    Legation’s suggestion that it revert to the method of shipping its imports into
                    Kiangsi Province under the protection of transit passes rather than under the
                        <hi rendition="#italic">pao-shang-piao</hi> system.</p>
                <p>There is also enclosed for the information of the Department a copy of the
                    Legation’s reply (No.1964) of today’s date, which seemed to be necessary in view
                    of the company’s apparent misunderstanding of the Legation’s position in this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paul S. Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d300-a1.xml" xpointer="d300-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d300-a2.xml" xpointer="d300-a2"/>
